Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, python3-yaml, python3-evdev, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, polkitd
Recommends: keyd (>= 2.5.0)
Suggests: xremap
Description: GUI remapper for the two mouse side buttons
 A small GTK4/libadwaita front end that writes side-button mappings for a single
 mouse device and applies them through one privileged helper behind polkit.
 It supports two back ends: keyd (long-press fires while the button is still held)
 and xremap (supports a double-tap gesture). Exactly one back end runs at a time,
 because both grab the device exclusively with EVIOCGRAB.
 .
 The GUI never polls devices and never blocks its main thread; applying is a
 single validated, backed-up, auto-rolled-back transaction.
